      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using `.loc` is often the preferred and more efficient method when you intend to modify a slice directly, as it avoids creating unnecessary copies. By using `df.loc[boolean_condition, 'new_column'] = values`, you are explicitly telling pandas to set values at specific locations, which handles the copying internally and avoids the warning. This approach is generally better for memory usage than creating a full copy if you are just making targeted modifications.",
